messages:
anya (platform): quick follow-up after RFC-218 — we need a concrete adapter capability matrix for Hosted / Dedicated / Private. who will own this? we should enumerate minimal fidelity guarantees per feature (streaming, kv cache, kernels, tracing, rollouts).

kevin (runtime): I can take a first pass. quick q: do we treat quantized kernels as 'compatible' or 'best-effort' for Private? my current view: Hosted = full kernel set guaranteed, Dedicated = subset guaranteed per SKU, Private = depends (opt-in shipping or best-effort).

maria (eng): +1. also call out observability: Hosted exposes per-request token attribution and traces; Private needs an opt-in agent/collector to forward traces or local-only retention.

trent (sre): ops constraints to capture: Dedicated must allow control-plane rollback for us to maintain safety without needing customer access. Private should default to customer-control for rollbacks unless contract says otherwise. Also define SLO downgrade semantics during fallback (e.g., fallback to minimal-latency vs minimal-cost).

sean (product): product POV: we need consistent request shapes and developer ergonomics. adapters should translate behind the scenes — not require app code changes. any feature toggles must be server-side and transparent.

kevin (runtime): propose a compact matrix approach. use a feature list like: `features: streaming|kv_cache|kernels|tracing|rollouts` and then statuses per environment: `guaranteed|best-effort|opt-in|unsupported`. example row: `Dedicated: streaming=guaranteed, kv_cache=guaranteed, kernels=guaranteed(specific skus), tracing=opt-in, rollouts=guaranteed`

anya (platform): perfect. can you sketch a proto-ish interface that adapters implement so we can autotest capability discovery? need something that reports capabilities at runtime.

kevin (runtime): sure. rough first pass: 
```
service Adapter {
  rpc Announce(Empty) returns (Capabilities) {}
}

message Capabilities {
  repeated string features = 1; // e.g., "streaming", "kv_cache"
  map<string,string> guarantees = 2; // feature->guarantee (guaranteed,best-effort,opt-in,unsupported)
}
```

maria (eng): small nit — avoid map for consumers that need deterministic ordering and stable schemas. recommend explicit repeated message: 
```
message Feature {
  string name = 1;
  string level = 2; // guaranteed,best-effort,opt-in,unsupported
}
message Capabilities {
  repeated Feature features = 1;
}
```

trent (sre): ops note: adapters must emit a health webhook or status event when capabilities change (e.g., `kv_cache` degraded). silent degradations have bitten us; alarms should be automatic when a guarantee flips from `guaranteed` -> `best-effort`.

deploy-bot: deploy started: feature-matrix-update -> staging (ci/1234)

anya (platform): next steps: kevin to open PR with matrix draft by EOD, maria to add observability/telemetry text, trent to enumerate alarm rules and runbook lines, sean to validate no API shims for developers. i'll collate into a single doc and link to RFC.

sean (product): ack. will validate with PMs that the matrix aligns with SLAs and packaging tiers.

kevin (runtime): noted. i'll include a compatibility matrix + sample adapter proto + test harness for capability assertions. will ping in this thread when draft is up.

anya (platform): thanks all. tagging @kevin (runtime) for visibility; @trent please add any historical incidents where capability drift caused outages so we can reference in runbooks. :thumbsup:
